DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: aayos po yung mga iba pa nating mga mas matitinding haharapin sa cyber security, social media, etc.

237
00:33:37,730 --> 00:33:43,370
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Sa mga kasama ko po sa DICT at ang mga attached agency, CICC, NPC, NTC,

238
00:33:45,510 --> 00:33:50,370
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: tumataas po ang kumpiyansa ko sa servisyo ng mga tao sa gobyerno.

239
00:33:52,350 --> 00:33:57,170
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Masisipag, magagalang, at professional po ang mga tao sa DICT.

240
00:33:57,330 --> 00:34:03,990
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Lahat po ay pwede nyo lapitan at lahat po ay hindi tatanggi sa pagsisilbi sa bayan.

241
00:34:05,550 --> 00:34:12,070
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Doon po sa ating mga kababayan, lalo na po yung mga matagal nang naghihintay ng connectivity.

242
00:34:13,090 --> 00:34:16,470
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Salamat po sa inyong pagtangkilik sa servisyo ng DICT.

243
00:34:17,030 --> 00:34:20,470
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Salamat po at alam namin naghintay kayo ng matagal.

244
00:34:20,470 --> 00:34:25,170
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: At kayo po ang dahilan kung bakit ngayong budget season na ito,

245
00:34:25,690 --> 00:34:31,650
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: bawat piso na hihingin namin sa Kongreso ay ilalaan namin sa pagsisilbisyo sa inyo.

246
00:34:32,570 --> 00:34:34,750
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Afterwards, with the permission of the Chair,

247
00:34:35,270 --> 00:34:40,950
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: I will now turn over the detailed presentation to our Undersecretary for Support Services,

248
00:34:41,470 --> 00:34:43,730
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Undersecretary Heherson Asiddao,

249
00:34:44,030 --> 00:34:48,650
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: who will present highlights of the Department's accomplishment in our proposed budget

250
00:34:48,650 --> 00:34:50,250
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: for Fiscal Year 2027

251
00:34:50,470 --> 00:34:53,410
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: that is embodied in our NEP.

252
00:34:53,790 --> 00:34:55,590
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Again, maraming maraming salamat po.

253
00:34:55,830 --> 00:34:56,970
Rep. Brian Poe: Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

254
00:34:57,470 --> 00:34:59,630
Rep. Brian Poe: Usec. Asiddao, you're recognized.

255
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:02,170
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Thank you very much, Sec. Henry.

256
00:35:02,830 --> 00:35:05,770
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: With your permission, Mr. Chair and the honorable members of this committee,

257
00:35:06,650 --> 00:35:08,170
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: a pleasant afternoon to everyone.

258
00:35:08,870 --> 00:35:12,850
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Allow us first to highlight some of the landmark accomplishments and reforms

259
00:35:12,850 --> 00:35:18,710
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: that are already translating our investments in ICT into tangible benefits for the Filipino people.

260
00:35:20,470 --> 00:35:28,270
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Mr. Chair, a copy of our full-page presentation is provided to each member of this committee for your perusal.

261
00:35:28,270 --> 00:35:34,030
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: I will go over the landmark accomplishments and at the same time the detailed NEP for 2027.

262
00:35:34,030 --> 00:35:39,670
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Mr. Chair, one of the most significant accomplishments is bringing government services

263
00:35:39,670 --> 00:35:44,030
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: directly into the hands of millions of Filipinos through the eGov Super App.

264
00:35:44,030 --> 00:35:48,630
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Today, we are proud to say that we have 61 million plus downloads,

265
00:35:49,790 --> 00:35:54,470
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: More than 56 million verified accounts and over 1.2 billion eGovDX transactions

266
00:35:54,470 --> 00:35:58,910
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: with 1,332 government e-services already integrated.

267
00:35:59,430 --> 00:36:07,390
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: These include everyday services such as PhilHealth, eTravel, eCov, eTrabajo, eLGU, and eReport,

268
00:36:07,970 --> 00:36:14,290
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: alongside more than 92 million digital national IDs issued and over 300 million digital ID transactions.

269
00:36:14,610 --> 00:36:19,770
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: More importantly, digital government is now institutionalized through the

270
00:36:19,790 --> 00:36:23,750
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: e-Governance Act and its Implementing Rules and Regulations.

271
00:36:23,750 --> 00:36:25,430
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Our direction is clear.

272
00:36:25,430 --> 00:36:28,230
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Instead of citizens having to navigate government,

273
00:36:28,230 --> 00:36:36,890
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: we are bringing government closer to the citizen through one increasingly integrated digital ecosystem.

274
00:36:36,890 --> 00:36:42,890
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Alongside expanding digital services, we have pursued reforms that make it faster and easier

275
00:36:42,890 --> 00:36:47,370
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: to build telecommunications infrastructure, ranging from streamlined permitting

276
00:36:47,370 --> 00:36:51,610
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: and longer regulatory validity to infrastructure sharing and open access.

277
00:36:51,970 --> 00:37:03,610
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: These reforms help enable expansion of telecommunications towers from close to 18,000 in 2020 to about 35,000 in 2023,

278
00:37:03,610 --> 00:37:13,610
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: while the number of connected Filipinos increased from 77 million in July 2022 to about 99 million by June of 2026.

279
00:37:13,610 --> 00:37:19,610
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: With the help of the Konektadong Pinoy Act, we are building on these gains by promoting greater competition,

280
00:37:19,610 --> 00:37:21,610
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: infrastructure sharing, and more efficient network deployment.

281
00:37:21,970 --> 00:37:24,890
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: The objective is straightforward.

282
00:37:25,710 --> 00:37:33,130
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: As government becomes more digital, connectivity must expand with it so more Filipinos can actually participate and benefit.

283
00:37:36,220 --> 00:37:43,240
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: These infrastructure and policy reforms are translating into measurable improvements in the everyday internet experience of Filipinos.

284
00:37:43,940 --> 00:37:50,800
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Since 2022, mobile download speeds have more than doubled, while fixed broadband speeds have also improved.

285
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:53,800
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: At the same time, Filipinos are getting significantly

286
00:37:54,180 --> 00:37:56,020
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: more data for every peso spent.

287
00:37:56,920 --> 00:37:59,920
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Most importantly, Mr. Chair, access is expanding.

288
00:37:59,920 --> 00:38:08,960
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: The share of Filipinos using internet increased from 25.4% in 2019 to about 67% in 2024,

289
00:38:09,420 --> 00:38:14,920
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: while households with internet access increased from 17.7% to about 48.8%.

290
00:38:15,580 --> 00:38:19,600
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: So the story across these first three accomplishments is connected.

291
00:38:20,360 --> 00:38:24,100
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: We are digitalizing government, removing barriers to connectivity,

292
00:38:24,180 --> 00:38:33,180
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: and working to ensure that faster and more affordable internet allows more Filipinos to actually participate in our digital transformation.

293
00:38:33,180 --> 00:38:40,180
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: And we are applying that same principle of digital transformation to improve specific government services.

294
00:38:40,180 --> 00:38:51,740
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: When better connectivity is paired with digital government, we can transform even very specific services that directly affect people's livelihoods.

295
00:38:51,740 --> 00:38:53,740
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: A good example is the PIMEDES portal,

296
00:38:53,740 --> 00:38:55,740
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Mr. Chair.

297
00:38:55,740 --> 00:39:02,060
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: What used to take an average of three months through a manual process can now be completed digitally in about five days.

298
00:39:02,740 --> 00:39:04,620
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: As of May 2026, Mr. Chair,

299
00:39:04,620 --> 00:39:09,730
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: 1,400 drivers have registered nationwide.

300
00:39:12,010 --> 00:39:17,930
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear] open [unclear] manual [unclear].

301
00:39:19,450 --> 00:39:26,860
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear] monthly [unclear] by [unclear]%.

302
00:39:26,860 --> 00:39:34,450
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear] 1,000 [unclear] 167 [unclear] digital [unclear].

303
00:39:39,410 --> 00:39:44,670
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear] spent on [unclear].

304
00:39:44,670 --> 00:39:47,470
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: More [unclear] services [unclear].

305
00:39:47,470 --> 00:39:50,870
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear] also ensure [unclear] environment [unclear].

306
00:39:50,870 --> 00:39:52,490
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear]

307
00:39:54,140 --> 00:39:56,860
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: As more services [unclear].

308
00:39:56,860 --> 00:39:58,900
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear]

309
00:39:58,900 --> 00:40:01,260
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear] even more [unclear].

310
00:40:01,260 --> 00:40:05,200
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: [unclear] center.

311
00:40:06,720 --> 00:40:11,020
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: We funded coverage from just 10 government agencies

312
00:40:11,020 --> 00:40:11,520
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: in 2022

313
00:40:11,520 --> 00:40:11,980
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: to 99

314
00:40:11,980 --> 00:40:14,400
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: agencies by August 2026,

315
00:40:14,400 --> 00:40:15,280
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: providing continuous

316
00:40:15,280 --> 00:40:16,280
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: cyber monitoring

317
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:19,700
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: across government.

318
00:40:19,700 --> 00:40:32,700
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: To date, Mr. Chair, the NSOC has monitored about 6.7 billion security alerts, demonstrating both the scale of threats we face and the importance of maintaining a strong national cyber defense capability.

319
00:40:32,700 --> 00:40:52,940
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Our investment in the next-generation hybrid NSOC will therefore sustain and strengthen 24-7 protection across disconnected agencies. Because our digital transformation can only succeed if Filipinos can also trust that the government systems and services they increasingly depend on are secure and resilient.

320
00:40:53,320 --> 00:41:02,810
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: But a secure and connected digital Philippines is only meaningful if Filipinos also have the skills to participate in it.

321
00:41:03,190 --> 00:41:04,830
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: From 2022 to 2026,

322
00:41:04,850 --> 00:41:25,190
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: DICT has reached about 695,000 Filipinos through free and accessible ICT capacity development, providing free training in areas such as AI, emerging technologies, cybersecurity, digital work, entrepreneurship, and digital literacy.

323
00:41:25,190 --> 00:41:34,830
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Through our DTCs, or Digital Transformation Centers, and initiatives such as SPARC, we are also bringing these opportunities closer to communities.

324
00:41:34,850 --> 00:41:41,570
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Including support that has helped form 35 local freelancer organizations nationwide.

325
00:41:42,670 --> 00:41:56,070
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Our goal is to complete the chain, connect our people, protect them online, equip them with relevant digital skills, and ultimately open more opportunities for work, enterprise, and participation in digital economy.

326
00:41:56,570 --> 00:42:05,840
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: As we expand these programs, we are also continuously improving how we deliver them.

327
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:08,280
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: A good example is our free public internet access program.

328
00:42:08,300 --> 00:42:25,880
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Through improved technology, contracting, and connectivity arrangement, we have achieved reported cost efficiencies of up to 70%, Mr. Chair, while continuing to expand access, particularly in geographically isolated and disadvantaged areas.

329
00:42:26,620 --> 00:42:35,240
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Today, free Wi-Fi has reached about 10.37 million unique beneficiaries with 127.49 million user sessions.

330
00:42:35,240 --> 00:42:43,120
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: At an estimated cost of about 22.4 pesos per unique beneficiary, and that's per month.

331
00:42:43,120 --> 00:42:45,540
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: This reflects how we want the ICT to work.

332
00:42:46,380 --> 00:42:57,580
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Expand what delivers, impact, measure performance, learn from implementation, and continuously find ways to deliver more value for every peso entrusted to us.

333
00:42:58,360 --> 00:43:01,020
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: And that is the principle we will carry moving forward.

334
00:43:01,020 --> 00:43:04,400
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Not simply to do more, but to do better.

335
00:43:05,080 --> 00:43:08,280
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: More efficiently, more effectively, and with greater success.

336
00:43:08,300 --> 00:43:09,860
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: And with greater impact for the Filipino people.

337
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:24,790
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Mr. Chair, I will now proceed to the Fiscal Year 2027 National Expenditure Program and present how the proposed budget will support the Department's priorities and commitments for the coming year.

338
00:43:26,170 --> 00:43:34,070
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: For the Fiscal Year 2027, the proposed budget for the ICT and its attached agencies totals 19.491 billion.

339
00:43:34,070 --> 00:43:39,970
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Of this amount, 17.6 billion is for the DICT Office of the Secretary.

340
00:43:40,190 --> 00:43:55,610
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: While 594.4 million is provided for CICC, 505.4 million for the National Privacy Commission, and 790 million for the National Telecommunications Commission.

341
00:43:56,170 --> 00:44:10,070
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Across the entire department, the budget consists of 1.692 billion for personal services, 13.9 billion for MOE, and 3.892 billion for capital outlay.

342
00:44:10,190 --> 00:44:20,090
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: In closing, Mr. Chair, and the honorable members of this committee, what we have presented today is more than a list of programs, targets, and budget figures.

343
00:44:20,090 --> 00:44:33,530
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Ito po ang direksyon ng DICT, mula connectivity, digital government, cybersecurity, digital skills, and jobs, hanggang sa pagbuo ng isang mas modernong gobyerno na tunay na naramdaman ng ating mga kababayan.

344
00:44:34,530 --> 00:44:40,030
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: With the support of the Congress for our Fiscal Year 2027 budget, we commit to translate every peso.

345
00:44:40,070 --> 00:44:50,730
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: entrusted to DICT into better connectivity, better digital services, greater digital opportunities, and concrete benefits for every Filipino.

346
00:44:51,330 --> 00:44:53,410
DICT Undersecretary for Support Services Heherson M. Asiddao: Maraming salamat po, and magandang hapon po sa inyong lahat.

347
00:44:55,660 --> 00:44:57,040
Rep. Brian Poe: Alright, maraming salamat po.

348
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:14,440
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay, with that, we will now go on to allowing our colleagues here to ask their questions of the department regarding the NEP for fiscal year 2027.

349
00:45:14,440 --> 00:45:24,580
Rep. Brian Poe: May I remind our distinguished colleagues that each member is allotted five minutes for questions or interpolation, excluding the response of the resource persons.

350
00:45:25,260 --> 00:45:29,540
Rep. Brian Poe: When the bell sounds, the member has 30 seconds to conclude.

351
00:45:29,540 --> 00:45:42,120
Rep. Brian Poe: Consistent with the long-standing practice of the House, the Chair shall recognize the minority, independent, and majority members in an alternating manner when practicable.

352
00:45:42,700 --> 00:45:50,400
Rep. Brian Poe: The Chair first recognizes the Honorable Renee Ko from the minority.

353
00:45:54,680 --> 00:45:56,560
Rep. Brian Poe: Ah, dapat, pero yung una nawala eh.

354
00:45:56,900 --> 00:45:59,900
Rep. Brian Poe: So, ladies first, as they say.

355
00:46:00,320 --> 00:46:01,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, thank you very much.

356
00:46:02,300 --> 00:46:02,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And good afternoon.

357
00:46:02,860 --> 00:46:06,460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Good afternoon to the Department of Information and Communication Technology.

358
00:46:07,480 --> 00:46:17,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My question would first be in relation to RA 10929, or the Free Public Internet Access Act.

359
00:46:18,220 --> 00:46:26,880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Last year, we took note of your report, and we also find it in the handout that the department gave us.

360
00:46:26,880 --> 00:46:32,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: That they targeted, or the department targeted, 10.2 million.

361
00:46:32,860 --> 00:46:41,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: individual beneficiaries for 2026, and then supposedly 4.5 million users for 2027.

362
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:47,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Can I check if that's correct?

363
00:46:47,340 --> 00:46:54,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: From last year, you mentioned that the target is 15.8 million individual beneficiaries.

364
00:46:54,720 --> 00:46:56,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This was set in 2025.

365
00:46:56,360 --> 00:47:02,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May I ask kung ano na pong progress, and ano pong nilalaman ng, supposedly, pag-targeting?

366
00:47:02,860 --> 00:47:08,580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng beneficiaris ng RA 10929 in this manner?

367
00:47:09,740 --> 00:47:24,620
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, I would like to ask my colleague, Asek Chris, to respond with a detailed answer for your question, if it's okay, Mr. Chair.

368
00:47:26,120 --> 00:47:27,540
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair.

369
00:47:28,320 --> 00:47:29,820
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes, you may be recognized.

370
00:47:29,820 --> 00:47:32,280
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair.

371
00:47:32,860 --> 00:47:59,620
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Currently, Mr. Chair, we have about 10.37 million unique users for the August 31 data, and that encompasses 11,836 different locations, composed of schools, markets, tourist spots, public places, barangay halls, and other public plazas, with 29,091 operational access points.

372
00:47:59,620 --> 00:48:00,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair.

373
00:48:00,700 --> 00:48:03,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Correct me if I'm wrong na lang.

374
00:48:05,220 --> 00:48:14,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Tinak-count niyo po kung ilan po yung nakakakonect sa free public internet, and yun yung characterization natin ng beneficiaris.

375
00:48:14,200 --> 00:48:15,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is this correct, Mr. Chair?

376
00:48:15,780 --> 00:48:16,520
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Yes, Mr. Chair.

377
00:48:17,380 --> 00:48:22,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Mr. Chair, last year, you mentioned na may 15.8 million target beneficiaris kayo.

378
00:48:23,200 --> 00:48:30,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, I assume because ang report niyo po ay 10.3 million this year, hindi po natin na-meet yung target na yun.

379
00:48:30,700 --> 00:48:33,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, can I ask po ba, paano niyo po ba ino-operationalize?

380
00:49:00,600 --> 00:49:02,640
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Ito nga po, ma'am. Patray nga po itong wireless.

381
00:49:03,000 --> 00:49:03,560
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Sorry po.

382
00:49:05,840 --> 00:49:07,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Connectivity issue, right now.

383
00:49:08,080 --> 00:49:08,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ayan, sige.

384
00:49:11,800 --> 00:49:18,200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ayan, so paano niyo po na may measure yung gusto nating 15 million na target beneficiaris?

385
00:49:18,200 --> 00:49:21,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Will you just add, essentially, access points?

386
00:49:21,300 --> 00:49:27,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And paano may ensure na yung additional 5 million ay maka-access to these access points?

387
00:49:30,650 --> 00:49:31,090
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Mr. Chair.

388
00:49:31,710 --> 00:49:37,650
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: For now po, we aim to achieve the 15 million unique users by the end of this year.

389
00:49:37,650 --> 00:49:47,690
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: So, we have a lot of projects right now that are in the pipeline and are nearing the post-qual evaluation and subsequent award.

390
00:49:48,090 --> 00:49:54,710
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: With this po, pag nag-start na po mag-deployment, we will be deploying additional access points in different locations

391
00:49:54,710 --> 00:50:00,870
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: that covers po yung mga public markets, tourist spots, and additional schools po.

392
00:50:01,170 --> 00:50:04,510
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Ati po mga rural health units po natin.

393
00:50:04,630 --> 00:50:09,530
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: So, that's how we aim to achieve yung 15 million target po natin.

394
00:50:09,950 --> 00:50:15,010
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, maintain po yung 15.8 million target beneficiaris for this year also?

395
00:50:15,650 --> 00:50:16,270
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Yes, Mr. Chair.

396
00:50:16,270 --> 00:50:18,710
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay, and by adding access points.

397
00:50:19,330 --> 00:50:29,390
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Can I ask po, because under the law, may minimum na sineset na sana po yung public basic education institutions and state universities and colleges ay makabitan.

398
00:50:29,910 --> 00:50:31,010
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Can I ask for...

399
00:50:31,010 --> 00:50:33,010
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Progress update po dito.

400
00:50:33,150 --> 00:50:34,250
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ilan po bang...

401
00:50:34,250 --> 00:50:39,570
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: How many percentage of public educational institutions and SUCs ang nakabitan na po natin?

402
00:50:41,740 --> 00:50:42,800
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Yung sa...

403
00:50:42,800 --> 00:50:43,480
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: For the...

404
00:50:43,480 --> 00:50:46,740
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Mr. Chair, yung for sa DepEd schools po muna unahin ko.

405
00:50:47,280 --> 00:50:50,100
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Yung sa schools connected po natin, based on our latest data,

406
00:50:50,560 --> 00:50:56,140
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: last August 31, 99.39% na po ang schools out,

407
00:50:56,280 --> 00:50:59,540
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: considering po yung mga DepEd schools na 45,328.

408
00:50:59,540 --> 00:51:01,620
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: So, 99.39% na po yung connected.

409
00:51:02,420 --> 00:51:03,740
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: And we also have yung...

410
00:51:03,740 --> 00:51:11,340
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Sa SUCs naman po, meron po tayong ongoing na project din po sa free Wi-Fi

411
00:51:11,340 --> 00:51:17,180
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: to connect po yung 220 state universities and colleges nationwide for Phase 1

412
00:51:17,180 --> 00:51:20,980
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: and then we'll connect the balance po by next year.

413
00:51:21,440 --> 00:51:21,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay.

414
00:51:22,160 --> 00:51:29,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pwede po bang makahingi ng list of schools and SUCs na hindi pa po nakakabitan?

415
00:51:29,720 --> 00:51:31,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And even yung priority markets?

416
00:51:32,420 --> 00:51:37,040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Or public areas na gustong kabitan para po ma-meet yung 15 million target?

417
00:51:37,880 --> 00:51:39,620
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Mr. Chair, we will comply, Mr. Chair.

418
00:51:40,120 --> 00:51:40,880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

419
00:51:41,160 --> 00:51:44,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, bilang principal author yung Kabataan Partylist,

420
00:51:44,480 --> 00:51:48,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: or one of the principal authors of what is now RA 10929,

421
00:51:48,700 --> 00:51:52,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: gusto po natin na continuously ay natche-check kung paano po na-implement ito

422
00:51:52,900 --> 00:51:57,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at paano nagiging beneficiary at nahahatid sa kabataan yung connectivity.

423
00:51:58,260 --> 00:52:02,400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Bilang at this point, bahagi na siya ng right to information.

424
00:52:02,420 --> 00:52:04,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Or freedom of access of information.

425
00:52:05,460 --> 00:52:10,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, my next question would be in relation to siguro pagpondo nito,

426
00:52:11,180 --> 00:52:13,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: magkano po yung pondo na nire-request?

427
00:52:13,300 --> 00:52:14,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is it still 5 million?

428
00:52:14,880 --> 00:52:16,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And is that 3% of the BESF?

429
00:52:19,900 --> 00:52:27,580
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: For free Wi-Fi, Mr. Chair, the request is about 5 billion pesos, Mr. Chair, from the SUF.

430
00:52:30,640 --> 00:52:33,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And siguro is that yung pinaka-request na po?

431
00:52:33,860 --> 00:52:34,540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kasi naalala ko lang.

432
00:52:34,560 --> 00:52:41,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Last year, 7.5 billion yung request for the Free Public Internet Access Act.

433
00:52:42,000 --> 00:52:44,780
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Mr. Chair, yung sa 5 billion po na-request,

434
00:52:45,000 --> 00:52:49,020
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: ito po yung will ensure na yung mga nakabitanan po natin ngayon ng locations,

435
00:52:49,160 --> 00:52:50,540
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: masusustain po natin siya for next.

436
00:52:51,000 --> 00:52:59,140
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: But if we're going to have to add more locations and add more schools na makukonektan pa,

437
00:52:59,140 --> 00:53:01,680
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: mapaprovide na natin ng libre connectivity na reliable,

438
00:53:02,640 --> 00:53:04,140
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: we will need to have...

439
00:53:04,560 --> 00:53:12,920
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: may synergy naman po kasi tayo with yung mga other NBP or other programs po ng DICT.

440
00:53:13,080 --> 00:53:16,740
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: Pero for free Wi-Fi, yung mas direct and mabilis pong impact is

441
00:53:16,740 --> 00:53:25,380
DICT Assistant Secretary Christian Mark G. Guingcangco: every peso po na-added sa FPF budget will really translate po agad sa last mile connectivity.

442
00:53:26,240 --> 00:53:26,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay, sige.

443
00:53:27,180 --> 00:53:33,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung may additional budget request na lang po in relation sa kung paano mas mapupondohan yung mga additional access,

444
00:53:34,560 --> 00:53:38,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: points ay pwede rin pong makareceive na lang through this committee ang representation na ito.

445
00:53:40,180 --> 00:53:44,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, my next question is in relation to social media registration,

446
00:53:45,260 --> 00:53:48,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: given na ito po ay isang mainit na usapin,

447
00:53:48,860 --> 00:53:52,800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: given po yung naging instances of violence in schools,

448
00:53:53,360 --> 00:53:57,000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na napadaloy po yung hindi lang communications,

449
00:53:57,000 --> 00:54:00,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: pero paano po nahubog sa ganong sitwasyon through social media.

450
00:54:01,340 --> 00:54:03,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At meron pong mga naging dialogues,

451
00:54:03,440 --> 00:54:04,000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ang DICT with...

452
00:54:04,560 --> 00:54:07,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: well, social media platforms like Meta,

453
00:54:08,000 --> 00:54:12,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung paano po ito kagawin and through at pagbibigay pa nga po ng national ID

454
00:54:12,820 --> 00:54:17,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: para po maikumpirma yung mga ilang detalye ng mga users dito.

455
00:54:18,140 --> 00:54:22,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And many rights groups are concerned about the implementation of social media registration in the country.

456
00:54:22,860 --> 00:54:29,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So pwede po bang makapag-share ang departamento ng specific plan and or facing of the implementation, Mr. Chair?

457
00:54:31,140 --> 00:54:32,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

458
00:54:33,180 --> 00:54:33,860
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: background,

459
00:54:34,560 --> 00:54:35,080
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: lang po,

460
00:54:35,540 --> 00:54:39,680
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: yung meeting na nangyari sa Singapore,

461
00:54:40,020 --> 00:54:44,580
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: kasama po natin si Congresswoman Matibag din to represent the House,

462
00:54:45,200 --> 00:54:48,840
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: nangyari between Meta and Roblox.

463
00:54:49,380 --> 00:54:51,780
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Sinama po natin doon ng National Privacy Commission,

464
00:54:52,060 --> 00:54:55,280
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: ang NTC, CICC, and NBI,

465
00:54:55,280 --> 00:54:56,860
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: as well as DepEd po.

466
00:54:57,240 --> 00:55:00,340
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Just as a background, the discussion was very comprehensive.

467
00:55:00,980 --> 00:55:02,160
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Marami pong napag-usapan,

468
00:55:02,580 --> 00:55:04,280
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: hindi lang naman yung identity violation,

469
00:55:04,560 --> 00:55:10,880
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: doon sa tanong nyo po na identity verification as it relates to the national ID.

470
00:55:11,820 --> 00:55:13,020
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Si Roblox kasi,

471
00:55:13,680 --> 00:55:17,140
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: karamihan ng mga stakeholder niya, mga bata.

472
00:55:18,180 --> 00:55:21,720
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Ang isang problema ni Roblox kasi is age verification.

473
00:55:21,720 --> 00:55:24,120
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Para lang ma-verify yung age nila,

474
00:55:24,980 --> 00:55:27,640
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: magpapa facial, I mean facial recognition.

475
00:55:28,000 --> 00:55:30,900
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Facial recognition, tapos yung software nila,

476
00:55:31,500 --> 00:55:33,400
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: plus minus one, two years.

477
00:55:34,560 --> 00:55:37,320
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: May tatlong klase kasi ng Roblox,

478
00:55:37,320 --> 00:55:39,320
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: meron yung nine and below,

479
00:55:39,320 --> 00:55:42,220
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: meron yung nine to sixteen, and sixteen and above.

480
00:55:43,680 --> 00:55:45,060
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Ang napag-usapan namin,

481
00:55:45,060 --> 00:55:49,320
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: paano mas magiging accurate yung age verification?

482
00:55:49,800 --> 00:55:54,260
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Meron kasing tinatawag na i-verify solution ang national ID.

483
00:55:54,820 --> 00:55:57,520
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: So kung nandoon na po ang national ID nyo,

484
00:55:57,520 --> 00:56:00,820
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: sa nandoon na ang national ID nyo,

485
00:56:00,820 --> 00:56:02,820
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: kahit nawala pa yung physical card,

486
00:56:02,820 --> 00:56:04,400
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: basta yung digital,

487
00:56:04,560 --> 00:56:08,320
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: biometrics nyo nandoon na sa Philippine Statistical Authority,

488
00:56:08,320 --> 00:56:10,320
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: pwede na sila mag-API call.

489
00:56:10,320 --> 00:56:14,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: So ang mangyari si Roblox, tatanungin si national ID,

490
00:56:14,560 --> 00:56:17,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: eto bang si Juan de la Cruz na sinasabing nine years old,

491
00:56:17,560 --> 00:56:20,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: na eto yung address niya, et cetera, siya ba yan?

492
00:56:20,560 --> 00:56:22,060
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mag-yes-no lang yun.

493
00:56:22,060 --> 00:56:27,060
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: So wala pong ililipat na personal information from PSA

494
00:56:27,060 --> 00:56:28,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: papunta sa Roblox.

495
00:56:28,560 --> 00:56:33,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Ang mangyayari lang is ibe-verify lang na tama yung tao na nagpa,

496
00:56:33,560 --> 00:56:34,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Siyempre pag

497
00:56:34,560 --> 00:56:37,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: sinabi niyang nine years old yan, Juan de la Cruz,

498
00:56:37,560 --> 00:56:41,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: tapos ang edad pala niya doon sa national ID 16,

499
00:56:41,560 --> 00:56:44,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: ang lalabas na sagot doon, no?

500
00:56:44,560 --> 00:56:47,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: So yun lang po yung gagwing ni Roblox.

501
00:56:47,560 --> 00:56:51,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Ngayon, kapag gumana po yan sa Roblox,

502
00:56:51,560 --> 00:56:55,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: yun naman ang sinasabi ni Meta na po pwede niyang gamitin

503
00:56:55,560 --> 00:56:59,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: as another tool para makapag-verify din po siya

504
00:56:59,560 --> 00:57:03,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: ng edad ng mga kabataan or iba pang mga information na baka,

505
00:57:03,560 --> 00:57:06,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: kailangan nilang makalap.

506
00:57:06,560 --> 00:57:11,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Ito naman po yung nakafocus on making sure na kung sino man yung user,

507
00:57:11,560 --> 00:57:14,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: age-appropriate yung content na makukuha niya po.

508
00:57:14,560 --> 00:57:15,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Your Honor.

509
00:57:15,560 --> 00:57:21,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, just today ay may essentially statement or update ang Meta.

510
00:57:21,560 --> 00:57:23,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sinabi niya may quote-unquote,

511
00:57:23,560 --> 00:57:27,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: technical complexity for integrating the Philippine national ID for user verification.

512
00:57:27,560 --> 00:57:31,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ano po ba yung dini-detail ng Meta dito na

513
00:57:31,560 --> 00:57:32,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kahirapan,

514
00:57:32,560 --> 00:57:33,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: if ever?

515
00:57:33,560 --> 00:57:35,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Yung sinabi naman nila eh, may intindihan po natin.

516
00:57:35,560 --> 00:57:37,560
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Hindi pa nila nagagawa yan anywhere in the world.

517
