5950
04:17:31,200 --> 04:17:36,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Lalo na pag walang interference, naka 200-250 Mbps for upload and download.

5951
04:17:36,200 --> 04:17:39,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And malaking tulong po ito para sa ating mga schools.

5952
04:17:39,200 --> 04:17:42,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Lalo na actually galing lang po ako sa DepEd.

5953
04:17:42,200 --> 04:17:49,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And ang ating learning crisis ay kailangan din talaga na may digital help para doon.

5954
04:17:49,200 --> 04:17:53,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: But I'd wanted to ask, I think, a rather basic question.

5955
04:17:53,200 --> 04:17:56,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I know that EO 119 has been signed for a data framework.

5956
04:17:56,200 --> 04:17:58,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Do we have

5957
04:17:58,200 --> 04:17:59,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: data standards

5958
04:17:59,200 --> 04:18:00,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: in our government?

5959
04:18:00,200 --> 04:18:02,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I know that DBM has UACS codes.

5960
04:18:02,200 --> 04:18:06,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: But is there a data standard for entire bureaucracy?

5961
04:18:06,200 --> 04:18:16,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, by next week, we will convene the technical working group for the EO 119.

5962
04:18:16,200 --> 04:18:20,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: That is an inter-agency technical working group.

5963
04:18:20,200 --> 04:18:24,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: And we will craft the standards, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

5964
04:18:24,200 --> 04:18:28,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: I was just looking sana kay USEC Sara kanina.

5965
04:18:28,200 --> 04:18:30,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Because she knows the details eh.

5966
04:18:30,200 --> 04:18:35,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: But the technical working group starts meeting this week.

5967
04:18:35,200 --> 04:18:39,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair, and thank you, Mr. Secretary.

5968
04:18:39,200 --> 04:18:45,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Now I wanted to ask, because data standards are important.

5969
04:18:45,200 --> 04:18:51,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: When we look at DBM as well, it should be, you know, may UACS yan, unified identifiers.

5970
04:18:51,200 --> 04:18:57,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Would we go from the formulation of the NEP to the MGA, to SAROs, disbursements?

5971
04:18:57,200 --> 04:19:07,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I mean, I used to trade in the crypto space.

5972
04:19:07,200 --> 04:19:13,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And I know, I'm a bit exposed about blockchain.

5973
04:19:13,200 --> 04:19:20,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And we all know that it is a ledger, a distributed ledger, that is encrypted by a cryptographic hash.

5974
04:19:20,200 --> 04:19:25,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I wanted to ask, because I know that this is being pushed as well.

5975
04:19:25,200 --> 04:19:26,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Do you think that...

5976
04:19:26,200 --> 04:19:36,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Kadena, which I am a co-author, do you believe that this is feasible for our government?

5977
04:19:36,200 --> 04:19:40,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And how much do you think it would cost?

5978
04:19:40,200 --> 04:19:49,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, I think the concept of Kadena, the CA, the Kadena bill, is feasible in our government.

5979
04:19:49,200 --> 04:19:54,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: As to the amount, I think it depends on how the legislature will craft the laws.

5980
04:19:54,200 --> 04:20:02,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Whether it's public chain, private chain, and the extent to which it will be implemented.

5981
04:20:02,200 --> 04:20:11,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: But I think whatever the amount is, if it achieves the objective of transparency in government, it will be worth it, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

5982
04:20:11,200 --> 04:20:17,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair and Mr. Secretary, do you believe that Kadena will solve corruption in the Philippines?

5983
04:20:17,200 --> 04:20:22,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, Kadena is a tool to curb corruption.

5984
04:20:22,200 --> 04:20:28,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: As with all transparency portals that we're implementing right now.

5985
04:20:28,200 --> 04:20:32,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Ultimately, it's how effective the tool is implemented.

5986
04:20:32,200 --> 04:20:36,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: I think it can minimize corruption.

5987
04:20:36,200 --> 04:20:39,200
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Definitely, it will increase transparency.

5988
04:20:39,200 --> 04:20:40,200
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Thank you.

5989
04:20:40,200 --> 04:20:49,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And when we talk about Kadena,

5990
04:20:49,500 --> 04:20:52,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: and it's supposed to curb corruption,

5991
04:20:52,500 --> 04:20:57,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: it's supposed to curb corruption, I understand.

5992
04:20:57,500 --> 04:21:03,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: But I know that Bayani Chain has also made on-chain for free.

5993
04:21:03,500 --> 04:21:06,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Do you believe that this is possible?

5994
04:21:06,500 --> 04:21:15,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: That we can also have a very minimal budget for this in case it does pass or in case that we do pursue it?

5995
04:21:15,500 --> 04:21:18,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

5996
04:21:18,500 --> 04:21:24,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: the one that Bayani Chain did was a free chain.

5997
04:21:24,500 --> 04:21:36,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Basically, what they did is just onboarded the published budget of 2025 into a public chain.

5998
04:21:36,500 --> 04:21:46,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: I think the approach of uploading the published budget on any chain is feasible and that's free.

5999
04:21:46,500 --> 04:21:52,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: The question there is if you establish a system end-to-end from NEP to expenditure.

6000
04:21:52,500 --> 04:21:55,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: And more importantly, which is I'm a big proponent of,

6001
04:21:55,500 --> 04:21:57,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: you use stable coin.

6002
04:21:57,500 --> 04:22:02,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Because if you want to track every peso that comes out of the government,

6003
04:22:02,500 --> 04:22:06,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: the easier way of doing it is to just tokenize all of the peso.

6004
04:22:06,500 --> 04:22:09,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: And then, you can now follow the provenance.

6005
04:22:09,500 --> 04:22:13,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Now, if that's the ambition that we want,

6006
04:22:13,500 --> 04:22:15,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: I think that would be the better solution.

6007
04:22:15,500 --> 04:22:20,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Because right now, each citizen can account for every peso that goes out of the government.

6008
04:22:20,500 --> 04:22:24,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: But it will take a lot of work, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

6009
04:22:24,500 --> 04:22:26,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So it seems, Mr. Chair and Mr. Secretary,

6010
04:22:26,500 --> 04:22:31,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: it seems that once we make it transparent,

6011
04:22:31,500 --> 04:22:38,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: it may have the same effect but we have to ensure that data going in is also as credible, correct?

6012
04:22:38,500 --> 04:22:42,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair, I'd like to ask about EGov.

6013
04:22:42,500 --> 04:22:44,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And I think I wanted to ask,

6014
04:22:45,500 --> 04:22:49,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: is this government-owned?

6015
04:22:49,500 --> 04:22:54,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Because I know that it collects government data and as well as citizens' data.

6016
04:22:54,500 --> 04:22:58,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Who owns EGov, the source code, Mr. Secretary?

6017
04:22:58,500 --> 04:23:02,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, the ownership is with the government.

6018
04:23:02,500 --> 04:23:08,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: I think earlier conversation, I have USEC Admiral who mentioned that

6019
04:23:08,500 --> 04:23:12,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: we're the custodian and owner of the source code at this point.

6020
04:23:12,500 --> 04:23:13,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay.

6021
04:23:13,500 --> 04:23:15,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And how many active monthly users?

6022
04:23:15,500 --> 04:23:20,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, maybe I should turn it over to USEC Admiral for the details

6023
04:23:20,500 --> 04:23:25,500
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: so that it's consistent with his earlier statement.

6024
04:23:25,500 --> 04:23:26,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay.

6025
04:23:26,500 --> 04:23:28,500
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: USEC, you may share the numbers once more?

6026
04:23:28,500 --> 04:23:29,500
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Yes, Mr. Chair.

6027
04:23:29,500 --> 04:23:30,500
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Let me answer that.

6028
04:23:30,500 --> 04:23:37,500
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So right now, Mr. Chair, since we already have 61 million downloads with 56 million unique users,

6029
04:23:37,500 --> 04:23:43,500
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: our average daily download, Mr. Chair, is about 70,000 to 100,000 a day.

6030
04:23:43,500 --> 04:23:44,500
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So that's the average download.

6031
04:23:44,500 --> 04:23:50,500
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So approximately, Mr. Chair, for monthly active downloads,

6032
04:23:50,500 --> 04:23:58,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: about around 3 million downloads monthly, Mr. Chair.

6033
04:23:58,550 --> 04:23:59,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay.

6034
04:23:59,550 --> 04:24:10,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair and USEC, how much is that per user, per transaction is the cost to run EGov?

6035
04:24:10,550 --> 04:24:15,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: In terms of maybe economic impact on the current budget that we have,

6036
04:24:15,550 --> 04:24:19,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: approximately, Mr. Chair, around 9 pesos per user, Mr. Chair.

6037
04:24:19,550 --> 04:24:20,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay.

6038
04:24:20,550 --> 04:24:23,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And how does EGov get funded?

6039
04:24:23,550 --> 04:24:27,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: For the development, Mr. Chair, since we build this internally,

6040
04:24:27,550 --> 04:24:31,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: so we don't have any contractor developing and building EGov.

6041
04:24:31,550 --> 04:24:33,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: It's an in-house developed platform.

6042
04:24:33,550 --> 04:24:38,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Right now, Mr. Chair, we're only paying our own staff to do it.

6043
04:24:38,550 --> 04:24:44,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Right now, we have about approximately more than 30 programmers

6044
04:24:44,550 --> 04:24:47,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: doing it, Mr. Chair.

6045
04:24:47,550 --> 04:24:53,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay. So, Mr. Chair, you said 9 pesos per user, correct?

6046
04:24:53,550 --> 04:24:59,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: For comparing our current budget, EGov budget, to the users, Mr. Chair.

6047
04:24:59,550 --> 04:25:04,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay. So all internal and no line item budget, correct?

6048
04:25:04,550 --> 04:25:09,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And there are no private companies or contractors working?

6049
04:25:09,550 --> 04:25:12,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Yes, Mr. Chair, for the development, for the R&amp;D.

6050
04:25:12,550 --> 04:25:16,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: The one that's only paying, Mr. Chair, is actually the subscription of our storage,

6051
04:25:16,550 --> 04:25:21,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: our cloud, service security, and other non-software developers' expenses.

6052
04:25:21,550 --> 04:25:24,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay. And where is this cloud stored?

6053
04:25:24,550 --> 04:25:27,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Right now, Mr. Chair, it's stored in Singapore.

6054
04:25:27,550 --> 04:25:31,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So since we're using public cloud services, Mr. Chair.

6055
04:25:31,550 --> 04:25:35,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay. So what company in Singapore, if I may ask?

6056
04:25:35,550 --> 04:25:38,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So we're using AWS, like 80%.

6057
04:25:38,550 --> 04:25:41,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: We also have several services stored in Google.

6058
04:25:41,550 --> 04:25:42,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay.

6059
04:25:42,550 --> 04:25:48,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: We have some in the Google Cloud and also some also in our current existing co-locations, Mr. Chair.

6060
04:25:48,550 --> 04:25:56,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay. Mr. Chair, so it seems that the data of our Filipino people are in AWS or Google Cloud in Singapore, no?

6061
04:25:56,550 --> 04:26:05,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair, I'd like to ask the department if are you amenable that we have sovereign data centers to house our data?

6062
04:26:05,550 --> 04:26:07,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: That's the ideal, Mr. Chair.

6063
04:26:07,550 --> 04:26:11,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So we're supposed to own it, manage it locally.

6064
04:26:11,550 --> 04:26:13,550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Locally, Mr. Chair.

6065
04:26:13,550 --> 04:26:14,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay. Thank you.

6066
04:26:14,550 --> 04:26:15,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: One last question.

6067
04:26:15,550 --> 04:26:17,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Alam kong time's up na rin ako.

6068
04:26:17,550 --> 04:26:25,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: But siguro dahil Department of Tourism is next, yung digital nomad visa na lang, ano po yung status po nun?

6069
04:26:25,550 --> 04:26:29,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Tsaka sana meron tayong mas maraming digital nomads na makapunta sa ating bansa.

6070
04:26:29,550 --> 04:26:32,550
Rep. Brian Poe: Great transition and buzzer beater.

6071
04:26:32,550 --> 04:26:34,550
Rep. Brian Poe: Who do I recognize from DICT?

6072
04:26:34,550 --> 04:26:35,550
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, your honor.

6073
04:26:35,550 --> 04:26:38,550
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Actually, we've been pushing the nomad visa.

6074
04:26:38,550 --> 04:26:40,550
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: And we've been working closely with DICT.

6075
04:26:40,550 --> 04:26:44,550
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Working closely with the Department of Foreign Affairs.

6076
04:26:44,550 --> 04:26:53,550
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: But the latest, I think, if I can pass it on to USEC Sarah on the latest status of that initiative.

6077
04:26:55,550 --> 04:26:57,550
DICT Undersecretary for Policy, Legal, and Communications Sarah Maria Q. Sison: With your permission, Mr. Chair.

6078
04:26:57,550 --> 04:27:08,550
DICT Undersecretary for Policy, Legal, and Communications Sarah Maria Q. Sison: So the Office of the Undersecretary for Policy is working closely with our Cybersecurity Bureau together with the Department of Foreign Affairs.

6079
04:27:08,550 --> 04:27:12,550
DICT Undersecretary for Policy, Legal, and Communications Sarah Maria Q. Sison: It is still in the planning and consultation stage.

6080
04:27:12,550 --> 04:27:20,550
DICT Undersecretary for Policy, Legal, and Communications Sarah Maria Q. Sison: But we will give an update as soon as we have our timeline because there's a lot of cybersecurity issues involved, Mr. Chair.

6081
04:27:20,550 --> 04:27:22,550
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay. Thank you so much.

6082
04:27:22,550 --> 04:27:29,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Thank you so much, Mr. Chair, and to the Department of Information, Communications, and Technology.

6083
04:27:29,550 --> 04:27:32,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I look forward to much more of your work.

6084
04:27:32,550 --> 04:27:36,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I'd like to congratulate Zach Henry and the whole DICT team.

6085
04:27:36,550 --> 04:27:40,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I believe that you have a track record.

6086
04:27:40,550 --> 04:27:49,550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And we hope that more budget for the DICT because here we are, dear colleagues, compared to our Asian and global partners.

6087
04:27:49,550 --> 04:27:50,550
Rep. Brian Poe: So, thank you so much.

6088
04:27:50,550 --> 04:27:54,550
Rep. Brian Poe: I need to just ask to make sure, Representative Tino.

6089
04:27:54,550 --> 04:27:56,550
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay.

6090
04:27:56,550 --> 04:27:57,550
Rep. Brian Poe: With that being said, Vice Chair?

6091
